WHAT WE COULD NOT VERIFY
------------------------

Upstream could not be fetched directly. `raw.githubusercontent.com` is denied by this
session's egress policy (403 on CONNECT, recorded by the proxy), and the repository was
not attached to the session. Everything sourced from upstream above came through a
summarizing fetch that returned verbatim extracts on request but declined to return
whole files.

Consequences, stated so a later reader does not have to rediscover them:

  - No upstream commit SHA is recorded. "Vendored from main" is unfalsifiable, and we
    will not write a SHA we did not read.
  - SKILL.md is NOT byte-comparable to upstream SKILL-mini.md and must not be diffed
    against it as if it were. It is our compression of v2, which is a different
    artifact reached by a different route.
  - Upstream SKILL.md, registry/, bridge/BRIDGE.md and assay.py were never read.

RECONCILING WITH UPSTREAM (NOT PLANNED)
---------------------------------------

Considered and declined on 2026-08-06: the attribution recorded above is sufficient, and
attaching the repo to chase a diff is not worth doing. See the Amendment section of
ADR-019. This is a reference for anyone who later wants the comparison — it is NOT
outstanding work, and it does not need doing before this package can be used or promoted.

If you do want it, attach the repo to a session, then compare and record the SHA:

    add_repo algocratic/the-algorithm-lite
    diff <upstream SKILL-mini.md> .claude/skills/the-algorithm-lite/SKILL.md

Expect real differences. The value of that diff is finding which rules upstream carries
that our compression dropped — not making the files match.
